In `checkIfIsAvailable` (packages/trpc/server/routers/viewer/slots.ts), the working-hours check computes both `start` and `end` from `slotStartTime`:
```ts
const start = slotStartTime.hour() * 60 + slotStartTime.minute();
const end = slotStartTime.hour() * 60 + slotStartTime.minute();
```
so `end` is always identical to `start`. This means `end > workingHour.endTime` will never reflect the slot's true end (which should be based on `slotEndTime` / `time.add(eventLength, ...)`). As a result, a slot that begins within working hours but extends beyond `workingHour.endTime` may be incorrectly treated as within working hours (and thus available).

